.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt POSTFIX-DANE-POLICY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm postfix-dane-policy
.Nd DANE-aware TLS policy socketmap service for Postfix
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -socket Ar path
.Op Fl -listen Ar address
.Op Fl -port Ar port
.Op Fl -allow-remote
.Op Fl -dns Ar address
.Op Fl -dns-port Ar port
.Op Fl -timeout Ar seconds
.Op Fl -lookup-budget Ar seconds
.Op Fl -max-connections Ar n
.Op Fl -mapname Ar name
.Op Fl -log Cm syslog | stderr
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
answers Postfix
.Va smtp_tls_policy_maps
lookups via the socketmap protocol.
For a next-hop domain whose MX RRset is DNSSEC-validated and where at
least one MX host publishes a DNSSEC-validated TLSA RRset for port 25
with at least one usable record (usage 2 or 3, selector 0 or 1,
matching type 0, 1 or 2), it returns
.Dq dane-only .
MX host names that are DNSSEC-validated aliases are expanded first, as
described in RFC 7672 section 2.2.2.
For every other domain it returns NOTFOUND, so the next policy map
(for example an MTA-STS resolver) or the global
.Va smtp_tls_security_level
applies.
DNS failures, DNSSEC validation failures and an exhausted lookup budget
return TEMP and Postfix defers the delivery instead of downgrading.
.Pp
Combined with
.Va smtp_tls_security_level = verify
this gives the policy
.Dq DANE if published, else MTA-STS, else a CA-verified certificate,
never plaintext.
.Pp
The service trusts the AD bit of the configured resolver and does not
validate DNSSEC itself.
The resolver must be a local, validating resolver such as
.Xr local_unbound 8 .
At startup and every 10 minutes the service checks that the resolver sets
the AD bit for the signed root zone; while that check fails every lookup
is answered with TEMP.
.Pp
Lookup keys are converted to A-labels (IDNA 2008, UTS#46); keys that are
not valid host names are answered with NOTFOUND without any DNS query.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -socket Ar path
Listen on a unix socket instead of TCP (recommended).
Access is controlled by the permissions of the containing directory.
.It Fl -listen Ar address
TCP listen address, IPv4 or IPv6.
Must be a loopback address unless
.Fl -allow-remote
is given.
Default: 127.0.0.1.
.It Fl -port Ar port
TCP listen port.
Default: 8462.
.It Fl -allow-remote
Allow a non-loopback
.Fl -listen
address.
The socketmap protocol has no authentication; do not use this.
.It Fl -dns Ar address
Validating DNS resolver.
Default: 127.0.0.1.
.It Fl -dns-port Ar port
Resolver port.
Default: 53.
.It Fl -timeout Ar seconds
DNS timeout per query.
Default: 5.
.It Fl -lookup-budget Ar seconds
Total time for one policy decision; exceeding it returns TEMP.
At most 10 MX hosts are checked.
Default: 20.
.It Fl -max-connections Ar n
Maximum number of concurrent client connections.
Default: 64.
.It Fl -mapname Ar name
Socketmap name expected in requests.
Default: dane.
.It Fl -log Cm syslog | stderr
Log destination.
Syslog uses the mail facility.
Default: syslog.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /var/run/postfix_dane_policy/policy.sock
Default socket of the rc.d script.
The directory belongs to the service user and the Postfix group, mode 0750.
.It Pa /var/run/postfix_dane_policy.pid
Pidfile of the
.Xr daemon 8
supervisor, owned by root.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pa main.cf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
smtp_tls_security_level = verify
smtp_dns_support_level = dnssec
smtp_tls_policy_maps =
    socketmap:unix:/var/run/postfix_dane_policy/policy.sock:dane,
    socketmap:inet:127.0.0.1:8461:mta-sts
smtp_tls_CAfile = /usr/local/share/certs/ca-root-nss.crt
tls_required_enable = no
smtp_tls_mandatory_protocols = >=TLSv1.2
.Ed
.Pp
.Va tls_required_enable
must be
.Dq no ,
otherwise a sender can disable the policy with a
.Dq TLS-Required: no
header (RFC 8689).
.Pp
.Pa rc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
postfix_dane_policy_enable="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Manual test:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
postmap -q posteo.de \e
    socketmap:unix:/var/run/postfix_dane_policy/policy.sock:dane
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr postconf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr local_unbound 8
.Rs
.%T RFC 7672: SMTP Security via Opportunistic DANE TLS
.Re
